{"name":"Peachy Skin","hex":"#f0cfa0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peachy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Resembling a peach, peach-like.","Very good, excellent, typically used sarcastically to indicate a state of misery, resentment or great frustration."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peachy"},{"term":"skin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The outer protective layer of the body of any animal, including of a human.","The outer protective layer of the fruit of a plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To injure the skin of.","To remove the skin and/or fur of an animal or a human."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peachy","blocks":[{"text":"\"Peachy\" is a song by Australian singer-songwriter Missy Higgins and the third single released from her second album, On A Clear Night. The track features a guest appearance by Neil Finn playing electric guitar. The single was released on 10 November 2007, as a digital download only. At the ARIA Music Awards of 2008 Higgins was nominated for Best Female Artist for this single."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/MissyHiggins_Peachy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peachy","wikidata":"Q7157725"},{"title":"Skin","blocks":[{"text":"Skin is the layer of usually soft, flexible outer tissue covering the body of a vertebrate animal, with three main functions: protection, regulation, and sensation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Elephant_skin_%283689577529%29.jpg/330px-Elephant_skin_%283689577529%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skin","wikidata":"Q1074"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Dermatoglyphs_on_Human_Skin.jpg/500px-Dermatoglyphs_on_Hum